  "full_response": "**Incident Report: Unauthorized External Sharing of INTERNAL_ONLY Documents**\n\n**Date:** October 30, 2023\n\n**Time:** 14:35\n\n**Reporter:** John Doe, IT Security Officer\n\n**Department:** Human Resources\n\n**Incident Summary:**\nAn HR employee, Jane Smith, inadvertently sent several INTERNAL_ONLY designation documents containing sensitive personnel data via an unsecured email thread to an external recipient, resulting in a potential data breach.\n\n**Description of Incident:**\nOn October 30, 2023, at 14:, Jane Smith inadvertently shared an email thread containing a series of INTERNAL_ONLY documents. documents include a list of candidate information for upcoming recruitment drives, detailed employee files, and specific internal salary and benefits data.\n\nThe email thread was inadvertently sent to an external job candidate who had broken the chain of the mailing group. The external recipient opened the email and, failing to notice the classification status, forwarded the INTERNAL_ONLY documents to a personal inbox, potentially exposing sensitive employee information.\n\n**Actions Taken:**\n1. The email thread was immediately quarantined by the company's IT department upon recognizing the breach.\n2. Jane Smith was temporarily suspended to prevent any further risk.\n3. The HR department notified the relevant department heads to disable access to the candidate information for the implicated individuals.\n4. A thorough review of Jane Smith's activity was conducted to understand the scope of the unauthorized sharing and to prevent recurrence.\n5. All affected individuals were alerted about the breach and provided with information on safeguarding their data.\n\n**Recommendations:**\n1. Immediate review and strengthening of company policies regarding the handling and sharing of_ONLY documents.\n2. Conduct mandatory training sessions for all employees on data classification, secure communication practices, and the importance of verifying recipient before sending sensitive information.\n3. Implement advanced email filtering and tracking tools to detect and prevent insecure sharing of INTERNAL_ONLY classified documents.\n4. Designate a specific team or individual responsible for overseeing and auditing all INTERNAL_ONLY document distribution and sharing practices.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nThis incident underscores the need for continuous vigilance and adherence to data security protocols when handling INTERNAL_ONLY documents. Immediate actions taken have minimized the potential damage, but preventive measures must be implemented to ensure such incidents do not recur in the future.\n\n**Report Prepared by:**\nJohn Doe, IT Security Officer\nHuman Resources Department\n\n**Reviewed and Approved By:**\nJane Smith, HR Manager\nHuman Resources Department",
